# API Integration

- One HTTP client in `lib/api` (fetch wrapper). Feature modules export functions like `getOrders()`, not raw `fetch` in components.
- Base URL from `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`. Send cookies (`credentials: "include"`) for Better Auth sessions.
- REST prefix: `/api/v1`. Resources:

`/customers` `/categories` `/menu-items` `/tables` `/orders` `/kitchen` `/payments` `/reservations` `/ingredients` `/inventory` `/reviews` `/notifications` `/analytics`

- Envelope: `{ success, data, message, error }`. Map HTTP 4xx/5xx into thrown errors the UI can show.
- Never put API secrets, Cloudinary keys, or webhook secrets in client code.
- Do not invent endpoints or permissions. UI hide/show is not authorization.
- Use Socket.IO later only for live kitchen/order boards; CRUD stays REST.

```javascript
export async function apiGet(path) {
  const res = await fetch(`${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/api/v1${path}`, {
    credentials: "include",
  });
  const body = await res.json();
  if (!res.ok || !body.success) {
    throw new Error(body.message || body.error || "Request failed");
  }
  return body;
}
```
